## /etc/tor/torrc -- INT OS-INT hardened Tor client configuration.
##
## This Tor is a client only. INT builds it without the relay module, so it
## cannot act as a relay, bridge, exit node or directory cache: do not add
## ORPort, DirPort, DirCache or BridgeRelay lines (Tor would refuse to start).
## The service is disabled by default; "sudo int-privacy tor on" starts it.

ClientOnly 1
ExitRelay 0

## Applications on this machine only. Point them at socks5h://127.0.0.1:9050
## so DNS is also resolved through Tor.
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1/32
SocksPolicy reject *

## No control port. If a controller (e.g. nyx) is really needed, use only
## localhost and cookie authentication, never a password or a public address:
#ControlPort 127.0.0.1:9051
#CookieAuthentication 1
#CookieAuthFile /run/tor/control.authcookie

## Created by systemd (StateDirectory=tor), owned by the tor user, mode 0700.
DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
AvoidDiskWrites 1

## Logs go to the journal; addresses are scrubbed.
Log notice stdout
SafeLogging 1
RunAsDaemon 0
